# What the mock-server image is allowed to see.
#
# Scoped deliberately: BuildKit prefers `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the repository root
# one, so nothing here changes any other build in the repo.
#
# The rule is deny-then-admit rather than a list of things to skip. A skip list was silently
# wrong every time someone added a cache directory, and the failure it hid was not cosmetic:
# the build context is the repository root, so `COPY . .` was dropping the host's 1.1 GB
# `.venv` — absolute paths, host interpreter and all — directly on top of the virtualenv
# `uv sync` had just built inside the image, along with 86 MB of `.git`.
*

# The package itself, and the metadata uv and hatchling read to install it. `README.md` and
# `LICENSE` are named by `pyproject.toml`, so the build fails outright without them — this
# list is what the backend reads, not a guess at what looks relevant.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src

# The app being served, including its `identity.local.json`.
!examples

# Compiled leftovers from a host-side run, which are never the image's to reuse.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
